loss":"Say","transliteration":"qul","verse_key":"6:66"},{"pos":7,"ar":"لَّسْتُ","en_gloss":"I am not","transliteration":"lastu","verse_key":"6:66"},{"pos":8,"ar":"عَلَيْكُم","en_gloss":"over you","transliteration":"ʿalaykum","verse_key":"6:66"},{"pos":9,"ar":"بِوَكِيلٍۢ","en_gloss":"a manager","transliteration":"biwakīlin","verse_key":"6:66"},{"pos":10,"ar":"٦٦","en_gloss":"(66)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"6:66"}]},{"verse_key":"6:67","surah":6,"ayah":67,"ar_uthmani":"لِّكُلِّ نَبَإٍ مُّسْتَقَرٌّ ۚ وَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُونَ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Every prophecy has its fixed time to be fulfilled: you will come to realize this.’","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"لِّكُلِّ","en_gloss":"For every","transliteration":"likulli","verse_key":"6:67"},{"pos":2,"ar":"نَبَإٍۢ","en_gloss":"news","transliteration":"naba-in","verse_key":"6:67"},{"pos":3,"ar":"مُّسْتَقَرٌّۭ ۚ","en_gloss":"(is) a fixed time","transliteration":"mus'taqarrun","verse_key":"6:67"},{"pos":4,"ar":"وَسَوْفَ","en_gloss":"and soon","transliteration":"wasawfa","verse_key":"6:67"},{"pos":5,"ar":"تَعْلَمُونَ","en_gloss":"you will know","transliteration":"taʿlamūna","verse_key":"6:67"},{"pos":6,"ar":"٦٧","en_gloss":"(67)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"6:67"}]},{"verse_key":"6:68","surah":6,"ayah":68,"ar_uthmani":"وَإِذَا رَأَيْتَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَخُوضُونَ فِىٓ ءَايَـٰتِنَا فَأَعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ حَتَّىٰ يَخُوضُوا۟ فِى حَدِيثٍ غَيْرِهِۦ ۚ وَإِمَّا يُنسِيَنَّكَ ٱلشَّيْطَـٰنُ فَلَا تَقْعُدْ بَعْدَ ٱلذِّكْرَىٰ مَعَ ٱلْقَوْمِ ٱلظَّـٰلِمِينَ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"When you come across people who speak with scorn about Our revelations, turn away from them until they move on to another topic. If Satan should make you forget, then, when you have remembered, do not sit with those who are doing wrong.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَإِذَا","en_gloss":"And when","transliteration":"wa-idhā","verse_key":"6:68"},{"pos":2,"ar":"رَأَيْتَ","en_gloss":"you see","transliteration":"ra-ayta","verse_key":"6:68"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ٱلَّذِينَ"